{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/solution/method.py | head -50'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Canonical initial numerical method. All geometry is computed from inputs.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nimport ot\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\n\ndef _label_cost(x,y,r,ry):\n    xx=torch.tensor(np.concatenate([x,r]),dtype=torch.float32)\n    yy=np.concatenate([y,ry+10])\n    W=np.zeros((20,20),dtype=np.float32)\n    loss=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,backend='tensorized')\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        for i in range(20):\n            for j in range(i+1,20):\n                if not (yy==i).any() or not (yy==j).any():\n                    raise ValueError('Initial batch lacks a label support')\n                W[i,j]=W[j,i]=float(loss(xx[yy==i],xx[yy==j]))\n    return W\n\ndef value(x,y,r,ry,seed=17,batch_size=1024):\n    torch.set_num_threads(2)\n    x=np.asarray(x,np.float32); r=np.asarray(r,np.float32)\n    y=np.asarray(y,np.int64); ry=np.asarray(ry,np.int64)\n    tx=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(x))) for i in range(0,len(x),batch_size)]\n    tr=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(r))) for i in range(0,len(r),batch_size)]\n    W=_label_cost(x[tx[0]],y[tx[0]],r[tr[0]],ry[tr[0]])\n    def cost(z1,z2):\n        d=torch.cdist(z1[:,:,:-1],z2[:,:,:-1]).square()/2\n        return d+torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(2),z2[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(1)]/2\n    potential=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,\n                         potentials=True,cost=cost,backend='tensorized')\n    F={}; batchcost=np.zeros((len(tx),len(tr)))\n    for i,idx in enumerate(tx):\n        for j,jdx in enumerate(tr):\n            a=x[idx];b=r[jdx]\n            C=cdist(a,b,'sqeuclidean')/2+W[y[idx,None],ry[jdx][None,:]+10]/2\n            P=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(idx)),ot.unif(len(jdx)),C/max(float(C.max()),1e-12),.1)\n            batchcost[i,j]=float(np.sum(P*C))/(len(idx)+len(jdx))\n            z1=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([a,y[idx]]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            z2=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([b,ry[jdx]+10]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            with torch.inference_mode(): f,_=potential(z1,z2)\n            f=f.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\n            F[i,j]=(f-f.mean())*len(f)/(len(f)-1)\n    Q=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)),ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                  batchcost/max(float(batchcost.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                  numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    residual=max(np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(1)-ot.unif(len(tx)))),\n                 np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(0)-ot.unif(len(tr)))))\n    if residual>1e-6: raise ValueError(f'Unconverged batch transport: {residual}')\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /tmp/research_notes.md 2>/dev/null || echo \"No research notes found\"'", "aggregated_output": "# Hierarchical Transport Valuation - Research Notes\n\n## Task Overview\n- 30 cases (5 seeds x 6 corruption types), N=3000 candidate, M=2000 reference, 10-dim embeddings\n- Labels 0-9, reference labels offset by +10\n- Target: minimize time while maintaining NRMSE <= 0.01, Spearman >= 0.999, top-quartile overlap >= 0.98\n\n## Baseline Method Analysis\n\nThe canonical method does:\n1. **_label_cost**: Compute W (20x20) pairwise Sinkhorn distances between all label classes using GeomLoss SamplesLoss on first batch only\n2. **Per-batch OT**: For each candidate batch x reference batch pair (up to 1024 each):\n   - cdist + W label costs → cost matrix C\n   - POT sinkhorn for coupling P, compute batchcost\n   - GeomLoss SamplesLoss with custom cost to get potentials f\n   - Store normalized F\n3. **Batch-level OT**: Sinkhorn on batchcost matrix (numItermax=10000, stopThr=1e-10, reg=0.01)\n4. **Aggregation**: Weighted sum of potentials using Q as weights\n\nKey optimization opportunities:\n- N=3000, batch_size=1024 → 3 candidate batches, 2 reference batches = 6 batch pairs\n- Each pair does full Sinkhorn (POT) + GeomLoss potentials\n- W is computed only from first batch - maybe can be simplified\n- The double Sinkhorn (POT + GeomLoss) per pair is expensive\n- Batch-level OT with very tight convergence (stopThr=1e-10)\n\n## Experiments\n\n### v0 - Baseline\n- Date: 2026-10-10\n- Status: Running initial baseline measurement\n- Expected: ~seconds per case\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
